{"name":"Salmon Nigiri","hex":"#f9906f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"salmon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of several species of fish, typically of the Salmoninae subfamily, brownish above with silvery sides and delicate pinkish-orange flesh; they ascend rivers to spawn.","A meal or dish made from this fish."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale pinkish-orange colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salmon"},{"term":"nigiri","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Regular sushi: a piece of raw fish (or other topping) on top of a small oblong brick of sticky white rice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nigiri"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sushi","blocks":[{"text":"Sushi  is a traditional Japanese dish made with vinegared rice , typically seasoned with sugar and salt, and combined with a variety of ingredients , such as seafood, vegetables, or meat; raw seafood is the most common, although some may be cooked. While sushi has numerous styles and presentations, the current defining component is the vinegared rice, also known as shari (しゃり), or sumeshi (酢飯)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Sushi_platter.jpg/330px-Sushi_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sushi","wikidata":"Q46383"},{"title":"Salmon","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon are any of several commercially important species of ray-finned fish that can live in either freshwater or saltwater from the genera Salmo and Oncorhynchus of the family Salmonidae, native to tributaries of the North Atlantic (Salmo) and North Pacific (Oncorhynchus) basins. Salmon is a colloquial or common name used for fish in this group, but is not a scientific name. Other closely related fish in the same family include trout, char, grayling, whitefish, lenok and taimen, all coldwater fish of the subarctic and cooler temperate regions with some sporadic endorheic populations in Central Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Salmo_salar.jpg/330px-Salmo_salar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon","wikidata":"Q2796766"},{"title":"Salmon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon is a warm color ranging from light orange to pink, named after the color of salmon flesh."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/SockeyeMaleCloseup_%2814522094556%29.jpg/330px-SockeyeMaleCloseup_%2814522094556%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2015138"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Barack_Obama_and_Shinzo_Abe_at_Sukyabashi_Jiro_April_2014.jpg/500px-Barack_Obama_and_Shinzo_Abe_at_Sukyabashi_Jiro_April_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Barack_Obama_and_Shinzo_Abe_at_Sukyabashi_Jiro_April_2014.jpg/1280px-Barack_Obama_and_Shinzo_Abe_at_Sukyabashi_Jiro_April_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Barack_Obama_and_Shinzo_Abe_at_Sukyabashi_Jiro_April_2014.jpg/500px-Barack_Obama_and_Shinzo_Abe_at_Sukyabashi_Jiro_April_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"President Barack Obama and Prime Minister Shinzo Abe at Sukiyabashi Jiro","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarack_Obama_and_Shinzo_Abe_at_Sukyabashi_Jiro_April_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Hiroshige_Bowl_of_Sushi.jpg/500px-Hiroshige_Bowl_of_Sushi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th